        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Urethral discharge"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Reports 3/7 of whitish urethral discharge, initially scant and now increased, especially in the mornings; described as 'not really pus'. Mild dried whitish discharge observed at the meatus."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-7",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-7",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Meatal examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Meatus slightly erythematous. No ulcers, vesicles, or warts."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-8",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Dysuria"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Reports mild dysuria."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-9",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-9",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Left testicular and scrotal pain"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Reports insidious onset 3/7 ago of constant dull left hemiscrotal/testicular pain, rated 4 or 5 out of 10. Worse with standing or walking and better lying down or with supportive underwear. Describes pain as tracking along the tube at the back, like the epididymis."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-10",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-10",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Associated reported symptoms and pertinent negatives"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Denies frank haematuria, fever, rigors, flank pain, nausea, vomiting, lower urinary tract symptoms, testicular lump, trauma, sudden onset or severe pain, weight loss, night sweats, abdominal pain, and change in bowel habit."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-11",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-11",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "General appearance"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Well appearing, no apparent distress; walking easily and conversant."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-12",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-12",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Abdominal examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Abdomen soft and non-tender, with no suprapubic or flank tenderness."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-13",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-13",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Penis and scrotal examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Penis with normal external appearance. Left hemiscrotum mildly swollen and warmer than the right, with posterior testicular/epididymal tenderness; left epididymis feels thickened and is tender, especially at the head and body. Right testis and epididymis normal and non-tender. No obvious masses."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-14",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-14",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Testicular position and cremasteric reflex"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Cremasteric reflex present bilaterally. No high-riding testis or horizontal lie."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-15",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-15",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Spermatic cord and inguinal examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Mild left spermatic cord tenderness. No varicocele or obvious hernia. No inguinal lymphadenopathy."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-16",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-16",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Perineal examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Perineum intact, with no erythema or induration."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-17",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-17",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Prostate and rectal examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Prostate mildly enlarged and smooth, non-tender, with no bogginess or marked tenderness. No perianal or rectal tenderness."
      }
    },
